{"parentUuid":"605b926f-24c1-43bf-9c79-6ef70d3ac3ae","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JByjnG51Dvp7Hv4aek2tpV","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SAT Competition 2024 cloud track parallel track Mallob Painless winner\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Results of SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/downloads/satcomp24slides.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - domschrei/mallob: Malleable Load Balancer. Massively Parallel Logic Backend. Award-winning SAT solving for the cloud.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/domschrei/mallob\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/results.html\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat and MallobSat-ImpCheck In the SAT Competition 2024 Dominik Schreiber\",\"url\":\"https://dominikschreiber.de/papers/2024-mallob.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel Clause Sharing Strategy Based on Graph Structure of SAT Problem\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol305-sat2024/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.17/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.17.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2020 - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0004370221001235\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat naps in the SAT Competition 2025 Dominik Schreiber\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/papers/2025-mallob-naps.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"D-Painless: A Framework for Distributed Portfolio SAT Solving | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-90653-4_3\"},{\"title\":\"The Results of SAT Competition 2020 Tom´aˇs Balyo, Nils Froleyks, Marijn Heule,\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2020/downloads/satcomp20slides.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2020\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2020/results.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the winners for SAT Competition 2024:\n\n**Cloud Track:**\nMallobSat by Dominik Schreiber won the Cloud Track with a PAR-2 score of 278.87 and solved 356 instances.\n\n**Parallel Track:**\nPainless by Mazigh Saoudi, Souheib Baarir, Julien Sopena, Thibault Lejemble, and Sabrine Saouli won the Parallel Track with a PAR-2 score of 447.99 and solved 174 instances. MallobSat came in second place in the Parallel Track with a PAR-2 score of 512.15 and 173 solved instances.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c176eb25-c882-41ce-9df0-b909345eadfa","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:39.057Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"605b926f-24c1-43bf-9c79-6ef70d3ac3ae","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"852f96b2-1cda-4bf3-9651-db545ab1c029","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017bvwmEJknXxN9Wp9cFkz56","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Mallob SAT solver 2025 release single machine multi-thread\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[2505.18836] Distributed Incremental SAT Solving with Mallob: Report and Case Study with Hierarchical Planning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.18836\"},{\"title\":\"Mallob in the SAT Competition 2022 - Dominik Schreiber\",\"url\":\"https://dominikschreiber.de/papers/2022-mallob.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - domschrei/mallob: Malleable Load Balancer. Massively Parallel Logic Backend. Award-winning SAT solving for the cloud.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/domschrei/mallob\"},{\"title\":\"mallob-mono in the SAT 2020 Cloud Track\",\"url\":\"https://dominikschreiber.de/papers/2020-mallob-mono.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · domschrei/mallob\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/domschrei/mallob/releases\"},{\"title\":\"D-Painless: A Framework for Distributed Portfolio SAT Solving | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-90653-4_3\"},{\"title\":\"Streamlining Distributed SAT Solver Design - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.27\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) PaMiraXT: Parallel SAT solving with threads and message passing\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220163285_PaMiraXT_Parallel_SAT_solving_with_threads_and_message_passing\"},{\"title\":\"From Scalable SAT to MaxSAT: Massively Parallel Solution Improving Search\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/papers/2025-socs-distributed-maxsat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[2205.06590] Scalable SAT Solving in the Cloud\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.06590\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Mallob SAT solver releases and multi-threading capabilities:\n\n## Recent Releases and Features\n\nRecent work describes an extension of the distributed job scheduling and SAT solving platform Mallob by incremental SAT solving, embedded in a case study on SAT-based hierarchical planning.\n\nThe latest releases include a modular architecture for easily adding new application engines to Mallob, a generic SatJobStream interface for applications to spawn (incremental) SAT tasks including a latency-hiding sequential solver thread, and a prototypical distributed MaxSAT engine.\n\n## Multi-threading Capabilities\n\nMallob can run with multiple processes and threads—for example, using Open MPI, you can run Mallob with a total of eight processes à four threads each. \n\nMallob uses the number of contained literals in a formula to decide on how many threads to spawn in each MPI process, providing adaptive multi-threading based on problem characteristics.\n\n## Single Machine Execution\n\nA special configuration called \"mallob-mono\" (mallob mono instance mode) was added to solve a single instance with full computational power from the beginning, which enables single-machine SAT solving with all available resources.\n\nThe 2025 research developments include improvements to clause sharing and distributed incremental SAT solving capabilities.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"30f972b8-7b2c-4220-810d-53ac1d83399d","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:39.561Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"852f96b2-1cda-4bf3-9651-db545ab1c029","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"bb270460-542c-497a-8344-d32e420e574d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VWVvzvQhzF15XMZjxoMK1n","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PaInleSS SAT solver 2025 IPASIR-2 clause sharing\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"IPASIR 2 Workgroup · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ipasir2\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ipasir2/ipasir2: IPASIR 2 Specification and Discussion\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ipasir2/ipasir2\"},{\"title\":\"D-Painless: A Framework for Distributed Portfolio SAT Solving | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-90653-4_3\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"PaInleSS: a Framework for Parallel SAT Solving. - LRDE\",\"url\":\"https://www.lrde.epita.fr/dload/papers/le-frioux.17.sat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - satlecture/kit2025: Lecture: Practical SAT Solving (ST 2025)\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/satlecture/kit2025\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat: Scalable SAT Solving by Clause Sharing\",\"url\":\"https://dominikschreiber.de/papers/2024-jair-mallobsat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"PaInleSS: A Framework for Parallel SAT Solving | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-66263-3_15\"},{\"title\":\"PaInleSS: A Framework for Parallel SAT Solving | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/318986849_PaInleSS_A_Framework_for_Parallel_SAT_Solving\"},{\"title\":\"Streamlining Distributed SAT Solver Design Dominik Schreiber # Ñ\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/SchreiberRigiLupertiBiere-SAT25.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about PaInleSS, SAT solver development, IPASIR-2, and clause sharing:\n\n## PaInleSS Framework\n\nPaInleSS is a framework to build parallel SAT solvers for many-core environments that provides the implementation of basics for parallel SAT solving like clause exchanges, Portfolio and Divide-and-Conquer strategies. It is a generic, modular, and efficient framework developed in C++11, allowing an easy implementation of parallel strategies and minimizes the effort to encode new parallelization and sharing strategies.\n\n## IPASIR-2 and Clause Sharing\n\nIn the typical parallel portfolio framework, SAT solvers exchange information in terms of learned clauses. Since IPASIR only supports the export of learned clauses, IPASIR-2 should also support the asynchronous import of clauses.\n\nTo cover both use cases, IPASIR-2 offers the possibility to register a function for importing a clause from an external source, such that the solver can control when and how to import clauses.\n\n## Recent Developments (2025)\n\nRecent work has extended PaInleSS for distributed settings. D-Painless is a new extension of the framework to include the distributed portfolio strategy and clause sharing, allowing the incorporation of various clause-sharing strategies and node topologies, resulting in a versatile framework that eases distributed SAT solvers development.\n\nA \"painless-2\" configuration won the Parallel track in SAT Competition 2024.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ad2a0de9-b5d8-4be4-a485-30c473acbef8","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:40.613Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bb270460-542c-497a-8344-d32e420e574d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
