{"parentUuid":"1a93321e-1512-42d2-9e36-a6d0d69cc1c7","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01SjBYwiHZiEofmSHto37JZ6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fu8YtTvVVVqH7MQb5kmDV4","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/domschrei/mallob","prompt":"From the README: Can Mallob run on a single machine without MPI/cluster? What's \"mallob-mono\"? Does it have a 24-thread shared-memory mode that's competitive with portfolio CDCL like Kissat-MAB? Build complexity for single-host use."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1011,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3511,"cache_read_input_tokens":27202,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3511,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CasshaCvM2viSAWevcMRk","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"6e8997a6-8d6e-4ee0-9fcc-86daab5fc721","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:50.978Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6e8997a6-8d6e-4ee0-9fcc-86daab5fc721","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01SjBYwiHZiEofmSHto37JZ6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012UVUBD6A981VyRV4GFcw3w","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/index.html","prompt":"Get full SAT Competition 2025 track listing and winner per track. Especially: parallel track top 3, cloud track top 3, sequential top 3. Note any new tracks vs 2024 (e.g. cloud-only, Mallob restricted, etc.)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1011,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3511,"cache_read_input_tokens":27202,"output_tokens":793,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3511},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1011,"output_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":27202,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3511,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3511,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CasshaCvM2viSAWevcMRk","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f5f8834a-9eff-437b-9bdf-0231c1d3c1cb","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:52.644Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"74ec6f7d-bad1-4095-8739-45ebe000a782","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YboxeiJcjDSMqSjXajZMvC","type":"tool_result","content":"# SAT Competition 2025 Results Summary\n\nBased on the provided content, here's what can be confirmed about the 2025 competition:\n\n**Parallel Track Winner:**\nMallobSat secured first place in the shared-memory parallel main track (64 threads), with \"**Painless-PRS-Kissat** by Saoudi et al.\" placing second overall.\n\n**Performance Metrics:**\nThe margin was narrow—only 3% separated the top two solvers using the PAR-2 evaluation metric. MallobSat excelled on unsatisfiable instances while Painless-PRS-Kissat performed better on satisfiable problems.\n\n**Cloud Track Changes:**\nThe article notes that the 2025 competition notably **did not include** the distributed \"Cloud\" track (1600 threads) that MallobSat had dominated consistently since 2020. This represents a significant structural change from previous years.\n\n**Design Approach:**\nRather than portfolio diversity, MallobSat employed \"minimal solver diversification (random seeds and variable phases only)\" combined with Kissat search threads and YalSAT stochastic local search components.\n\n**Limitations:**\nThe provided content focuses on parallel track results and doesn't detail comprehensive cloud/cluster comparisons, new solver entrants, or specific 2024 versus 2025 performance shifts beyond noting the track restructuring."}]},"uuid":"0c56efbe-86c9-4cd0-906f-0dde4e9aeab1","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:52.756Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"74ec6f7d-bad1-4095-8739-45ebe000a782","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1a93321e-1512-42d2-9e36-a6d0d69cc1c7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AQwLThPvsp3wce5rBZr374","type":"tool_result","content":"# Mallob Recent Releases\n\nBased on the GitHub releases page, here are the most recent releases:\n\n## v2.0.0 (31 Jul)\n**Key Changes:**\n- Dual licensing: LGPL and MIT options\n- Enhanced clause sharing with \"unlimited sharing of units\"\n- Updated SAT solver backends (CaDiCaL, Kissat)\n- \"Low-latency support for distributed incremental SAT solving\"\n- New MaxSAT engine with parallel interval search\n- Experimental SMT solving via Bitwuzla\n- Modular architecture for application engines\n- Improved memory management and resource handling\n\n## v1.1.0 (23 Jul)\n**Key Changes:**\n- Documentation updates\n- New test suite for stable features\n- Bug fix for malleable clause exchange\n\n## v1.0.0 (29 Jun)\n**Key Changes:**\n- First tagged release\n- Stable for malleable job scheduling of non-incremental SAT tasks\n- Incremental SAT solving marked as experimental\n\n---\n\n**Note:** The page content provided does not contain information about single-machine multi-thread mode, \"mallob-mono,\" non-MPI builds, IPASIR-2 support, or \"low cadence\"/\"WAN\" geographic clause sharing. Only the distributed incremental SAT improvements mentioned above are visible in the release notes."}]},"uuid":"09342a90-e59f-4326-9fa6-40b98efb79e9","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:53.117Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1a93321e-1512-42d2-9e36-a6d0d69cc1c7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6e8997a6-8d6e-4ee0-9fcc-86daab5fc721","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fu8YtTvVVVqH7MQb5kmDV4","type":"tool_result","content":"# Mallob Single-Machine Capability\n\nBased on the README, Mallob **can run on a single machine**. The documentation explicitly mentions a \"mono\" mode:\n\n> \"to run MallobSat with a single (MPI) process with twelve Kissat threads, execute `build/mallob -mono=path/to/problem.cnf`\"\n\nThis indicates the `-mono` flag enables single-process execution without requiring a cluster setup.\n\nHowever, the provided README doesn't directly address whether this shared-memory configuration rivals portfolio solvers like Kissat-MAB in competitive performance. The document emphasizes Mallob's **distributed capabilities** and achievements in parallel competitions rather than single-machine benchmarks.\n\nFor details on build complexity and single-host optimization specifics, the README directs readers to `docs/setup.md` and `docs/execute.md`, which aren't included in this excerpt. These documentation files would contain the technical details about compilation options and performance considerations for non-distributed use cases."}]},"uuid":"faec62c6-f2e4-4c95-9772-4e73b5ee21e0","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:55.826Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6e8997a6-8d6e-4ee0-9fcc-86daab5fc721","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f5f8834a-9eff-437b-9bdf-0231c1d3c1cb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012UVUBD6A981VyRV4GFcw3w","type":"tool_result","content":"# SAT Competition 2025 Track Information\n\nBased on the provided content, I can only confirm **two tracks** are mentioned:\n\n1. **Main Track**\n2. **Parallel Track**\n\n## Limitations of Available Information\n\nThe webpage does not include:\n- Final rankings or winners for any track\n- Top 3 placements in parallel or sequential categories\n- Information about a \"cloud track\"\n- Details comparing new vs. 2024 tracks\n- Specifics about \"Mallob restricted\" tracks\n\nThe page notes that \"The slides of the SAT Competition 2025 results are available\" (dated 2025-08-16), but the actual results content is not provided in the source material. You would need to access the PDF slides directly or visit the full competition website to obtain winner information and track comparisons with prior years."}]},"uuid":"50f4d98d-0d93-443a-b36f-cbd35e1051c5","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:00.949Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f5f8834a-9eff-437b-9bdf-0231c1d3c1cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
