{"parentUuid":"1034b6d3-8544-44f0-8410-d7f6d1878d4c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GUHgDGPX1whGD8tNh24MG2","type":"tool_result","content":"I cannot provide a meaningful summary of the MallobSat 2025 paper based on the content provided. The material appears to be raw PDF binary data without readable text content that would allow me to extract:\n\n- Details about NAPS\n- Single-machine vs. cluster performance numbers\n- Hardware specifications for parallel experiments\n- Thread count information\n- Benchmark comparisons with OR-Tools CP-SAT or Kissat-MAB\n\nTo assist you effectively, please provide either:\n1. The paper text in plain format\n2. A properly converted PDF with extractable text\n3. A direct link to the paper\n\nThis would enable me to deliver the specific technical comparisons and metrics you're requesting while maintaining the citation standards you've outlined.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 96.8KB) also saved to /home/zhuran24/.claude/projects/-home-zhuran24-claude-pj-zmd/7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9/tool-results/webfetch-1778369891395-q1cb9v.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"7569d51f-f803-48c3-97d7-b352b0c7c0f6","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:16.168Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1034b6d3-8544-44f0-8410-d7f6d1878d4c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"07b15d32-838f-4624-8b75-45e4c41d13ec","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K9sGzYbQrV18VUZGRKN9T6","type":"tool_result","content":"# IPASIR-2 Status and Implementation\n\n## Standardization Status\nBased on the repository content, IPASIR-2 remains in **draft/proposal stage as of the provided information**. The README explicitly states: \"We are pleased to present a draft that fulfills most of the above wishes.\" The project invites community feedback through discussions rather than announcing finalization.\n\n## Solver Implementations\nThe webpage provides **no information** about which specific solvers (Kissat, CaDiCaL, Glucose, etc.) have implemented IPASIR-2. The repository focuses on specification design rather than documenting adopters.\n\n## Clause Import/Export for Portfolio Sharing\nYes, IPASIR-2 does standardize this capability. The specification includes \"Clause Import\" functionality designed specifically for parallel clause-sharing portfolios. As documented: \"clauses which are exported by other solvers are asynchronously made available for import\" in distributed solving scenarios.\n\nThe interface supports different redundancy pledges (equivalence-preserving, satisfiability-preserving, or none) to accommodate various use cases beyond simple portfolio sharing.\n\n## Recent Activity\nThe repository shows **124 total commits** on the main branch, but the provided content doesn't display specific commit dates or recent activity timestamps needed to assess current development pace as of 2025."}]},"uuid":"1f0dbed9-6abb-4ca9-9bcf-914d11b1bfa8","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:16.335Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"07b15d32-838f-4624-8b75-45e4c41d13ec","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"61b05a78-9ef1-4430-9a71-79608d76eefe","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EJVHqf24tNafGr94BSTH1c","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT vs Kissat parallel portfolio 24 threads benchmark 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Results of SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/satcomp25slides.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel search problem in CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/i3TF_Szuz_k\"},{\"title\":\"Parallelism and multi threads\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/n1pAIfAQs7I\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solver - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SAT_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Split-BDD Multiplier Verification Benchmarks Submitted to ...\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereKonradKaufmannScholl-SAT-Competition-2025-benchmarks.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Solver Max - Well, that escalated quickly: OR-Tools\",\"url\":\"https://www.solvermax.com/blog/well-that-escalated-quickly-or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"arXiv:2504.14506v1 [math.OC] 20 Apr 2025 On Solving the Set Covering Problem\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.14506\"}]\n\nI found relevant search results about 2025 SAT competition benchmarks. The SAT Competition 2025 results show parallel track benchmarks with solvers including Kissat variants (MallobSAT, PL-PRS-GASPI-Kissat, PL-PRS-Kissat, and others), though OR-Tools CP-SAT is not mentioned in the parallel track results.\n\nHowever, I should note that the search results don't contain a direct comparison of OR-Tools CP-SAT versus Kissat parallel portfolio specifically for 24 threads. The SAT Competition 2025 results document shows Kissat-based parallel solvers performed well in the parallel track, but doesn't provide detailed benchmark data comparing them directly against OR-Tools CP-SAT with 24 thread configurations.\n\nFor a more specific benchmark comparison with 24 threads, you might want to:\n1. Check the full SAT Competition 2025 documentation directly\n2. Look for research papers or technical reports that specifically benchmark these solvers\n3. Review the solver documentation pages for their own benchmark results\n\nWould you like me to search for more specific information about any particular aspect of these solvers?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1f950c8b-94e5-408c-9238-217a83fd0444","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:17.932Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"61b05a78-9ef1-4430-9a71-79608d76eefe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
