{"parentUuid":"5d4547aa-5600-413f-8e0c-ca608058e004","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sg2iZT1j1m3RyXEh1TvYrv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"mallob-mono\" single machine 64 cores benchmarks vs Kissat-MAB parallel\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - domschrei/mallob: Malleable Load Balancer. Massively Parallel Logic Backend. Award-winning SAT solving for the cloud.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/domschrei/mallob\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2020 - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0004370221001235\"},{\"title\":\"NAS Parallel Benchmarks\",\"url\":\"https://www.nas.nasa.gov/software/npb.html\"},{\"title\":\"Benchmarking parallel programming for single-board computers - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0167739X24003650\"},{\"title\":\"Scalable SAT Solving in the Cloud | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-80223-3_35\"},{\"title\":\"Processor Benchmarks - Geekbench Browser\",\"url\":\"https://browser.geekbench.com/processor-benchmarks\"},{\"title\":\"mallob/README.md at master · domschrei/mallob\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/domschrei/mallob/blob/master/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · domschrei/mallob\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/domschrei/mallob/releases\"},{\"title\":\"Benchmarking Parallel Performance on Many-Core Processors | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-05215-1_3\"},{\"title\":\"PassMark CPU Benchmarks - Multithreaded - All - Page 1\",\"url\":\"https://www.cpubenchmark.net/multithread/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information comparing Mallob-Mono with other SAT solvers:\n\nMallob-Mono was able to solve more instances in 1000 seconds than the winner of the Parallel Track in 5000 seconds, which shows the potential of distributed SAT solving. This comparison was from the SAT Competition 2020.\n\nRegarding performance on 64 cores specifically, the best parallel solver used 32 threads on the 64 virtual cores that were available, as using fewer threads than the number of available virtual cores can be helpful since threads compete for memory and using all virtual cores may be detrimental to overall performance.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific benchmark comparisons between Mallob-Mono on 64 cores versus Kissat-MAB in terms of detailed performance metrics. The information available is primarily from the SAT Competition 2020, and more recent benchmark data comparing these specific configurations would require additional searches or access to competition papers and technical reports.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7ccdcaa2-b3a0-433c-8b40-d720db8c69f0","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:29.330Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5d4547aa-5600-413f-8e0c-ca608058e004","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ccfb4bd2-fdf1-4eb0-b42e-fa03ce8e1d9c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DH48ZmVzJfrtSJgerDneiG","type":"tool_result","content":"I apologize, but I cannot extract the requested information from the provided content. The material appears to be a PDF file containing compressed/encoded data rather than readable text about SAT Competition 2025.\n\nTo help you effectively, I would need:\n\n1. **Plain text or structured data** about the competition results\n2. **Clear ranking tables** showing solver performance metrics\n3. **Hardware specifications** listed in readable format\n4. **Participant lists** comparing 2024 and 2025 entries\n\n**What I can tell you:** The provided file shows binary PDF stream data that would require proper decompression and rendering to extract competition statistics, rankings, and participant information.\n\n**Suggestion:** Please provide either:\n- A text export of the slides\n- A markdown summary of key results\n- Direct links to official SAT Competition 2025 results pages\n- Screenshots of relevant ranking/participant tables\n\nOnce you share readable content, I'll be happy to extract the parallel track rankings, top-5 sequential solvers, hardware specifications, cloud track information, and comparative participant data.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 1MB) also saved to /home/zhuran24/.claude/projects/-home-zhuran24-claude-pj-zmd/7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9/tool-results/webfetch-1778369904309-6iu1u4.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"2d21f0d8-1bff-4648-a484-d9dc5d4cc8e2","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:29.699Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ccfb4bd2-fdf1-4eb0-b42e-fa03ce8e1d9c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2ad1aa6c-8179-4a90-b21c-17dfcd74088e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HdtBY5HxQJeEJCFsWPgy1b","type":"tool_result","content":"# Distributed Incremental SAT Solving with Mallob\n\n**Paper Summary:**\nThis 2025 arXiv report by Dominik Schreiber describes extensions to Mallob, a distributed platform for scheduling and SAT solving. The work introduces \"a low-latency interface for incremental jobs and specifically for IPASIR-style incremental SAT solving to Mallob.\"\n\n**Key Findings:**\nThe researchers tested their approach by processing 587 planning instances simultaneously across 2,348 cores. They observed \"significant speedups for several planning domains where SAT solving constitutes a major part of the planner's running time.\"\n\n**Significance:**\nThe authors suggest their distributed incremental SAT solving method \"may be useful for a wide range of SAT applications,\" indicating potential beyond the hierarchical planning case study they examined.\n\n**Classification:**\nThe paper falls under Distributed, Parallel, and Cluster Computing (cs.DC) and Logic in Computer Science (cs.LO).\n\n**Access:**\nAvailable as PDF, HTML, and TeX source via arXiv (2505.18836), submitted May 24, 2025."}]},"uuid":"d677c85d-ad7f-4725-919b-ba5cfc0529a7","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:30.570Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2ad1aa6c-8179-4a90-b21c-17dfcd74088e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d677c85d-ad7f-4725-919b-ba5cfc0529a7","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XhwWBoWEKtCcJ1sQB1z3gb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"已经够画像了。最后查一项 IPASIR-2 在 CaDiCaL/Kissat 的实装状态——决定 P3 watchlist。"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2358,"cache_read_input_tokens":37457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2358,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CassmGeMQfFkpkph5gwDc","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"0af116a5-17e5-4f73-ac88-8eb301a749dc","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:34.783Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0af116a5-17e5-4f73-ac88-8eb301a749dc","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XhwWBoWEKtCcJ1sQB1z3gb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L7TDW1gTHtK345w29moMRg","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CaDiCaL Kissat IPASIR-2 implementation 2025 clause import release"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2358,"cache_read_input_tokens":37457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2358,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CassmGeMQfFkpkph5gwDc","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"d89f4b81-4926-4511-8882-219fd561f371","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:34.851Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d89f4b81-4926-4511-8882-219fd561f371","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L7TDW1gTHtK345w29moMRg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CaDiCaL Kissat IPASIR-2 implementation 2025 clause import release\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - ipasir2/ipasir2_solver_cadical: CaDiCaL SAT Solver with IPASIR 2 Support · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ipasir2/ipasir2_solver_cadical\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR 2 Workgroup · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ipasir2\"},{\"title\":\"RustSAT: A Library for SAT Solving in Rust Christoph Jabs # Ñ\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol341-sat2025/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.15/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.15.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - arminbiere/kissat · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat\"},{\"title\":\"cadical/NEWS.md at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/NEWS.md\"},{\"title\":\"FreshPorts -- math/kissat: Kissat SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://www.freshports.org/math/kissat/\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/releases\"},{\"title\":\"rustsat::solvers - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/rustsat/latest/rustsat/solvers/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL 2.0 | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-65627-9_7\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL, Gimsatul, IsaSAT and Kissat Entering the SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2025-solvers.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding CaDiCaL, Kissat, and IPASIR-2 implementation related to clause import:\n\n## Overview\n\nIPASIR is a Re-entrant Incremental SAT solver API, and IPASIR-2 introduces asynchronous clause import alongside a configuration interface. IPASIR-2 should support the asynchronous import of clauses, expanding on the original IPASIR which only supported clause export.\n\n## Solvers Involved\n\nKissat is a \"keep it simple and clean bare metal SAT solver\" written in C and is a port of CaDiCaL back to C with improved data structures, better scheduling of inprocessing and optimized algorithms.\n\nThe goal of CaDiCaL's development was to obtain a CDCL solver which is easy to understand and change, while at the same time not being much slower than other state-of-the-art CDCL solvers.\n\n## Recent Updates (2025)\n\nA new version of CaDiCaL is available on the development branch on GitHub with code base increased from roughly 46 KLOC to 64 KLOC of C++, incorporating techniques ported from Kissat.\n\nThe search results indicate active development of IPASIR-2 support and integration of advanced features between these solvers, though specific details about clause import release dates in 2025 are not fully detailed in the available sources.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cbab7707-568f-4165-bf69-7ec992b1c572","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:38:41.461Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d89f4b81-4926-4511-8882-219fd561f371","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cbab7707-568f-4165-bf69-7ec992b1c572","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"af55dd10eeeac5fd0","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01EUNuNmeAHTPfM9D4XWohUs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"(忽略 task tools 提醒。) 数据已经够。给结论。\n\n---\n\n## SAT Comp 2025 主要变化\n- **Parallel track（共享内存 64 thread）冠军 MallobSat**（KIT, Schreiber），Painless-PRS-Kissat（Saoudi 等）第二，PAR-2 差距仅 ~3%。Mallob UNSAT 强、Painless SAT 强。\n- **Cloud track（1600 thread 集群）2025 取消** —— Mallob 自 2020 以来连冠 5 届的赛道直接没了，组委会结构性削减。意味着 SAT 社区未来重心回到\"单机厚机器\"而非超大集群。\n- 主/sequential track 仍是 CaDiCaL / Kissat / Gimsatul 等 Biere 系，2024→2025 没有颠覆性新人。\n- 跟 2024 对比：2024 Painless 拿 parallel 冠军、Mallob 拿 cloud；2025 Mallob 反夺 parallel、cloud 没了——格局收敛到\"Mallob vs Painless 二马\"。\n\n## Mallob 半年进展\n- **v2.0.0（2025-07-31）** 是关键 release：双许可（LGPL+MIT）、unlimited unit clause sharing、模块化 application engine、低延迟分布式 incremental SAT、实验性 MaxSAT 与 Bitwuzla SMT 引擎。\n- **`mallob-mono` 模式** 单 MPI 进程跑多 Kissat thread，可在单机不开集群用，README 直接给 `-mono=path/to/problem.cnf` 命令。但 Mallob 强项是**集群线性扩展**，单机 24 thread 没有公开 head-to-head 数据证明能干赢 Kissat-MAB / Painless-PRS（也没有跟 OR-Tools CP-SAT 比的 benchmark）。\n- 2025 arXiv 2505.18836：587 planning instance 跨 2,348 core 跑——还是大集群定位。\n\n## D-Painless / IPASIR-2\n- D-Painless（lip6, 2025 SAT 会议）把 Painless 框架扩到分布式 portfolio，可插拔 clause-sharing 策略和 node 拓扑，但论文需 Springer 登录没拿到细节。**没有公开\"WAN 低 cadence（5–10 min）clause exchange\"协议** —— 现有 LAN 假设是毫秒级 broadcast/ring。\n- **IPASIR-2 仍是 draft**，repo 124 commits、CaDiCaL 有官方实验分支 `ipasir2_solver_cadical`，Kissat 没看到合并。IPASIR-2 标准化\"异步 clause import\"，是 portfolio 互操作的未来基础但还没尘埃落定。\n\n## 跟项目契合\n- **替换 OR-Tools 主 solver：不可行**。LBBD / 整数/多商品流不是纯 SAT；Mallob/Painless 是 CNF SAT solver，不带 CP-SAT 的整数变量、线性约束、cumulative、circuit 等 global constraint。换主 solver 等于推翻整套 master/binding/routing/flow 模型，成本天文 + 收益不明。\n- **作为 binding/routing/flow 子问题 SAT 沙盒（D' / D'' / D'''）**：理论可行——把子问题 CNF-encode 后丢 mallob-mono 跑，跟 OR-Tools CP-SAT 对照。但门槛高：需要写 encode 层、需要把 SAT 答案 lift 回 CP 域、需要管 incremental（IPASIR 还没 finalized）。**ROI 偏低**，除非某个子问题被实测出 CP-SAT 跑得很差。\n- **跟 P2 #27（远程机 WAN）契合**：**目前不契合**。Mallob/D-Painless 的 clause-sharing 都假设 LAN 毫秒延迟；没有现成\"5–10 min cadence\"WAN 协议。如果硬上，需要自己写一层 clause filter（只交换 LBD≤3 的 unit / binary glue）+ batched compress/transmit——这是个独立研究项目，不是引第三方库的事。\n\n## verdict\n- **路线图新增 P2 / P3 条目：仅 P3 watchlist，不进 P2**。\n- **推荐 watchlist 项**（每 6 个月扫一次即可，不投人力）：\n  1. **IPASIR-2 finalization 时间线** —— 一旦 1.0 正式 + Kissat/CaDiCaL 都实装，重新评估\"OR-Tools CP-SAT worker 之间换 Kissat 引擎\"的可行性（OR-Tools 团队若跟进）。\n  2. **mallob-mono v2.x 单机 benchmark** —— 如果 KIT 出 24/32 thread vs 共享内存 portfolio 的对比数字，再决定要不要做\"binding 子问题 SAT 沙盒\"。\n  3. **WAN clause exchange 学术工作** —— 关键词：\"geo-distributed SAT\" / \"wide-area portfolio\"。目前空白；若有人发表，P2 #27 可借鉴。\n- **当前阶段不动作**：OR-Tools CP-SAT 8 worker 内置 portfolio + 内进程 clause sharing 仍是单机 24 thread 最实用的选择，跟前次 R1/R9 调研结论一致——半年内没有\"应当切换\"的信号。\n\nSources:\n- [SAT Competition 2025](https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/index.html)\n- [KIT MallobSat 2025 first place announcement](https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/news/2025-08-15-satcomp/)\n- [SAT Competition 2025 results slides PDF](https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/satcomp25slides.pdf)\n- [Mallob GitHub repo](https://github.com/domschrei/mallob)\n- [Mallob releases (v2.0.0 2025-07-31)](https://github.com/domschrei/mallob/releases)\n- [Distributed Incremental SAT with Mallob (arXiv 2505.18836)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.18836)\n- [MallobSat-NAPS in SAT Competition 2025 paper](https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/papers/2025-mallob-naps.pdf)\n- [SAT Competition 2024 results](https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/results.html)\n- [D-Painless paper (Springer)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-90653-4_3)\n- [IPASIR-2 spec repo](https://github.com/ipasir2/ipasir2)\n- [CaDiCaL with IPASIR-2 support](https://github.com/ipasir2/ipasir2_solver_cadical)\n- [CaDiCaL/Kissat SAT Comp 2025 entry paper](https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2025-solvers.pdf)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1495,"cache_read_input_tokens":39815,"output_tokens":2481,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1495},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2481,"cache_read_input_tokens":39815,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1495,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1495,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Cassn4hHULFArJwxLtSQ6","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"3961de88-6660-41a9-8d9f-3ce0bc2a66f4","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:39:29.262Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
